WEBVTT

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.650
Grandma...

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.350
You were in the video too, Baron.
This was 4 years ago, y'know.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.190
Grandma was doing fine back then...

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.270
I guess I shouldn't expect anything.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:31.740
I'll write you, Haruka-chan.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.710
I'm sure she's forgotten it.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:38.220
- Hey, there.
- Morning, Haruka-chan.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.720
Good morning, Kooriyama-san, Uchida-san.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.990
Are you expecting a letter
from somebody?

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.820
Oh, not really.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:49.590
I just remembered
something from the old days.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:52.960
Wow, your old days are my recent ones.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:53.900
Huh?

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.660
Once you're an adult
you tend to forget more...

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.470
than you remember.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.070
Did you forget a lot of stuff,
Kooriyama-san?

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.440
Have you ever forgotten about somebody
who was important to you?

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.970
I dunno about that...

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.150
I've had a long life so far,
and I've met lots of people...

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.690
so I'm sure I've forgotten
someone along the way.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.550
I won't forget.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:21.680
I won't forget about you.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.320
Thanks, little lady.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.490
Ai, what's up?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.670
Really? So, everyone's coming?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.270
Yeah. Uh-huh. Oh, really?

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.710
See ya.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.740
Hold on a second.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.410
Um, didn't you come here for a reason?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.540
Nah, we just came to see
how you were doing.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.700
Right, Uchida-chan?

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.380
Yes.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:50.190
Come to think of it, Haruka-chan,
has anything unusual happened recently?

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.790
Anything unusual?

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:57.090
It's all been really weird,
so I've kinda gotten used to it.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:01.070
That's incredible. I keep
feeling like my heart's gonna stop.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.200
Call us if anything happens.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.210
If there's anything we can do,
we'll help you.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.160
Thank you so much.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.510
Buh-bye.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.780
Oh, hello? Sorry!

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.150
Okay, I got it. Around 10 o'clock?

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.210
I'm glad she seems to be doing okay.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:25.180
Despite all the horrible things
that are happening.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:29.900
Kids have better adaptability
than adults.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.990
What is it, Uchida-chan?

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.310
That thing yesterday...

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.000
They've swept it under the carpet
as a meteorological phenomenon.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:40.170
That qualifies as a mirage?

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.380
Doesn't that upset you, Kooriyama-san?

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:46.710
It sounds like something
an adult would think of.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.340
Yes, but...

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.420
Even if we are killed,
we can ignore it if we have to.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.960
Kooriyama-san?

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:08.560
Oh, it's nothing. I just recalled
something after talking to the girl.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.430
So, what do we do now?

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.440
I'll speak directly
with Chairman Sasaki.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.810
And ask him to call off
the Magic Circle?

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:21.010
Uchida-chan, I've been thinking.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.920
When we were kids, we lived
using only our senses, right?

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.710
Then when we grew up,
we learned how society functions...

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.720
and then we learned to live
using only our intelligence. I think...

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.940
That thing yesterday
was definitely impossible.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.690
But it really was there.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:43.500
Of course it was.
We all saw it with our own eyes.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.970
Yeah, but it doesn't show up
on our cell phones...

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:48.410
It's a ghost! It was a gigantic ghost!

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.210
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.410
Do you think everyone forgot about it?

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.810
Forgot?

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.710
Everyone's stopped
talking about it, right?

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:00.780
All the adults really
hate talking about it.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.920
Maybe, but we definitely saw it.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.120
The next time it shows up,
I'll take it with THIS.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.490
Then they'd know it's real.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:09.180
Yuu...

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.930
Let's go out for ice cream.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.710
Yeah. Let's go, guys!

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.470
Yuu's been really happy recently.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:22.010
Maybe that's why.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:23.680
You brought it with you?

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:26.040
I'll get it with this camera
next time for sure.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.410
Can something like
that make someone happy?

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.150
Well, you get happy
with just a soccer ball...

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.430
This flower is pretty.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:01.690
What was that for?
It's not fair to the flower.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:05.110
I aimed at your head,
so why did I hit the flower?

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.410
I dunno.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:11.750
You...

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.620
Talk! What are you plotting?!

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:24.230
What? What do you mean?

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:26.940
Don't play dumb. Talk!

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.130
It hurts. It hurts...

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:34.780
Stop it, Kosagi!

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:39.600
Let go! He dodged my attack!
He's regained his senses!

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.150
Then why isn't he dodging you now?!

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.220
If Atori was sane, he would
have fought back already!

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:54.930
You okay, Atori?

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:58.900
It hurts. It hurts...

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:12.350
So do you really intend to approve
the Magic Circle Project, Professor?

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:15.910
This is wrong, Professor Sasaki!

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.850
Uchida, you haven't changed
a bit from since you were a student.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.390
You always jump to conclusions.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:25.260
Science isn't about conclusions...

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.460
It's not about conclusions,
it's about the process.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.400
You drilled that into me
all through university.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:33.460
You also told me that science
is the asset of all mankind.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:35.300
That it wasn't to be
used for profiteering.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:38.070
True, Uchida...

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:42.010
but from the moment we realize
that very science can be lucrative...

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:44.950
economics starts to make its influence.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.680
But professor!

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.580
I'll talk with Shinohara one more time.

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:53.300
Professor...

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.020
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:57.930
This doesn't mean
I believe your description...

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:02.770
of the critical outbreak of
the overlapping of dimensions...

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:05.100
as described in your report.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:10.420
I merely want to watch over the extent
of your research a little longer.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:14.080
Thank you so much, professor.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:22.810
Shut down the Magic Circle Project?

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.370
Sasaki-san, are you quite sane?

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:29.180
An abnormality in the quantum
potential has been recognized.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:32.490
As a member of the Absolute Critical
Prevention Planning Committee...

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:36.160
I cannot approve Magic Circle Project's
marine experiment under those conditions...

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.450
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah...

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.900
You seem to have the wrong idea.

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:45.020
Ab-com is merely a decoration.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.740
The government's excuse...

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:50.810
so they can claim that they're thinking
of people's safety and the environment.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:54.220
Perhaps you should consider
who you should thank...

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:57.750
for being able to spend time
in a monastical laboratory.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.390
However...

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:04.260
We're going to use this to pry open
the door of quantum mechanics.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.480
It will result in a new revolution
of the network.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:11.730
And it won't be just communications,
it will change the entire world.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:15.950
It's the time of change.
We will create a new world!

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.220
Under what authority are
you telling me to call it off?!

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.940
I didn't say you should call it off.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:26.250
I'm asking you to
momentarily rethink the project.

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:30.190
What's this? That sounds awfully weak.

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.990
That's true cause if we stop this now...

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:37.220
you won't get any funding for your labs.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:42.800
Forget this rethinking garbage
and let's go full force on this.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.730
The Mayuzumi interpretation of quantum
mechanics will be proven you know.

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:49.840
I cannot do that. I can't approve...

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:54.210
an experiment that is highly dangerous!

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:00.940
Going to the pool might be fun.

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:04.010
But it would be lame having
to wear our school swimsuits.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.690
I get sick swallowing the water.

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:09.130
Yeah, 'cause you're a bad swimmer.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:13.520
That's fine! There's no need to
force myself to go in the water!

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.590
I can live just fine on dry land!

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:16.860
Excuses, excuses!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.000
How pathetic!

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:18.970
What did you say?!

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:20.740
Ok, chill out, Fujiwara.

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.440
Haruka, what is it?

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:25.350
Aya-chan?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.880
Haruka? Hey, where
are you going, Haruka?

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:38.650
Aya-chan? You're Aya-chan, aren't you?

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:39.620
Huh?

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.130
Oh, it's Mrs. Mayuzumi's little Haruka!

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.860
It's been a long time.
How have you been?

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:51.860
Hello, it's nice to see you.
Are you here on vacation?

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.730
We're sightseeing because
it's summer break.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:56.270
Really...

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.000
Doesn't this take you back, Aya?

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:05.780
She was really lonely
when you moved from Tokyo.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:07.650
Y-Yeah.

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:13.430
Haruka-chan, please
write her letters again, okay?

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:15.000
Sure!

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:18.710
Mom, who is that girl?

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:28.430
Haruka-chan, are you really moving away?

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:29.460
Yeah.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.840
Okay, I'll write you letters!

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:33.040
Really?

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:35.310
Really! I promise!

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.090
Great!

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:48.120
Is she a friend from
when you lived in Tokyo?

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:52.620
Yeah. It's Aya-chan.
She's totally forgotten about me.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:58.630
Don't let it get you down, Haruka!
You have us now!

00:12:58.670 --> 00:12:59.870
It's not that.

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.630
It's not really bothering me.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.970
I was just a little surprised, that's all.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.580
Who cares about her anyway?
Our friendship, however, is eternal!

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:13.980
It will never end!

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.950
You'd be the first to forget.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:19.080
What did you say?!
That's rude, Fujiwara! Grr!

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:23.060
Oh, I forgot! My mom
asked me to pick up a few things.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:23.620
Huh?

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.690
Sorry, I gotta go now.

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:27.290
Hey, Haruka?

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.860
- This is bad.
- What do you mean?

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.100
I'm talking about Haruka!

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:34.870
What're you talking about?
She has an errand.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:39.150
You really do have a thick head.
She's lying about the errand, d'uh!

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.140
What? Really?

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:43.340
I think she took it hard.

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:46.020
I'll go and check on her.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.040
Yeah. Knowing her...

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.660
she'd get even more depressed
if we all go see her.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.380
Yeah.

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:09.370
I will perform a fixed reverse
calculation on the Dragon Torque.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.870
Wh-What did you just say?

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.350
A fixed reverse calculation?!

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:17.840
Correct.

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:21.050
We have Dragon Torque's
quantum composition data on file.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.450
If I recompose its REIZU
according to that data...

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:26.690
I can bring the Dragon Torque
to La'cryma.

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:27.800
Out of the question!

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:30.420
A fixed reverse calculation...

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:34.960
will require the full calculating power
of La'cryma's REIZU simulator!

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:38.100
The limes would be temporarily lost.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:41.470
What if Shangri-la were
to attack at that moment!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:45.010
Then is there a better solution?

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:54.150
I will perform the fixed reverse
calculation. Is that acceptable?

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.790
Good afternoon!

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.750
Come on in. Oh...

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:03.260
Haruka is out right now.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.290
Okay, is it okay if we wait for her?

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.290
Sure. You can wait in her room.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.360
Aye, aye!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.760
And the snacks and juice
are in the usual place.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.640
Yes, Kooriyama speaking.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:37.820
I've been ordered to end my assignment.

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:38.830
Huh?

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.090
They want me to get back.

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:45.240
Guess I'm not your bodyguard anymore.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:46.840
What do you mean?

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:50.590
Chairman Sasaki of Ab-Com has resigned.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.970
His replacement, a geezer named Tobe...

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:56.380
is going to remove you from Ab-Com.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:58.600
No way...

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:01.210
It's the usual dirty method.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.900
Marutai has moved to platform 3.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:20.170
Six to Three. Do you have confirmation?

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.470
Three to Six, Confirmed.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:34.490
Six to Three, Confirmed. Don't rush it.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:38.180
Hey, Detective.

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:48.510
Did you enjoy the almond jelly?

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:54.770
Why, you...

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:00.450
Somebody fell on the tracks!

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:09.880
Aida...

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:11.850
Where are you, Aida?!

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:16.760
Aida, hang on...

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:29.640
They covered up the
murder of my colleague...

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:32.340
by labeling it an impulsive suicide.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:34.510
Didn't the police investigate it properly?

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:38.110
The case was a spy incident going up
as high as a resident ambassador.

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:40.700
We couldn't make it public knowledge.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.510
That's awful.

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:48.220
Where are you going?

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:51.960
Even if we leak this to the media,
Shinohara will just hush it up.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.020
Most likely.

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:06.570
I'm not gonna give up this time.
I won't quit even if it will kill me.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:08.210
What?

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:09.810
Let's go, Uchida-chan.

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:13.650
All we can do right now
is to find Dr. Mayuzumi.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:40.140
I was starting to forget...
about Grandma.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:45.410
But I loved her so much, too.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:49.210
I guess I'm gonna
gradually forget her smile...

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:52.550
and her voice each day.

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:55.750
Wow, that's cute!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.400
Thanks, Grandma!

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:04.840
Your grandmother died
2 years ago, right?

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.700
You can't help it. It's hard
to keep remembering people...

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:10.730
who have passed away.

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.540
So everyone forgets.

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:16.660
Like how Aya-chan forgot about me.

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:20.450
Like how I forgot about grandma.

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:24.180
There are some things
that you won't forget.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:25.550
Huh?

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:30.930
I still remember how I first
met you like it was yesterday.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.800
It was summer break in second grade.

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:37.500
You came to my house
with Baron and your mom.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.840
You've forgotten, haven't you?

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.980
Man, you're so forgetful.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:50.650
No, I'm not. I remember it.

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:54.170
I totally remember it.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:58.880
I was so nervous because
we just moved to this town...

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:03.130
So I was really happy
when you were nice to me.

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:08.260
Let's head back.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:11.900
The gang will be waiting
for us at your place.

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:13.740
Yeah.

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:20.390
You held my hand back then too.

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:23.510
You only remember the stupid details.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.640
Commencing fixed reverse calculation.

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:30.650
Undulation function
approaching free values.

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:34.290
Probability rate rising
at 1.00% per second.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:37.090
Fix rate rising 0.2 per second.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:39.630
Commence data redirect!

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.160
Commence dimension transfer countdown!

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:54.310
Come on, Dragon Torque...

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:58.300
You're all here.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.520
This is really cool!

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:02.820
Fujiwara, don't get in the way.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.720
I won't. Hey, Tobi? What was that just now?

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:07.780
Isami, don't touch it...

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:08.740
Knock it off!

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:11.450
Atori, would you like to go up
to the mountain sometime?

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:14.040
Yeah. That might be fun.

00:21:15.470 --> 00:21:17.100
Where's Karasu?

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:20.130
He went to check out an area with
a high rate of dimensional change.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.640
What's wrong, Atori?

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:29.600
Atori?

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:32.780
This is bad. This is really bad.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:36.120
The wind is howling.

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:38.340
Tobi!

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:40.260
Atori?

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:42.860
What is this?

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.070
Fixed reverse calculation
rate at 72 percent.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:50.100
Huh? What is this?

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:52.100
Blue snow?!

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:53.150
Impossible.

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:54.670
Fixed reverse calculation?!

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:56.170
What the heck is that?

00:21:56.640 --> 00:22:00.670
It's Kuina. He's trying to take Haruka
back with him to La'cryma.

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:03.660
The dimension is wavering!

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:07.380
Karasu, this undulation...
I've never felt this kind of pressure!

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:12.890
Is it La'cryma?

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:16.160
Haruka!

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:17.730
Karasu!

00:22:21.830 --> 00:22:23.430
- Hey!
- Ow...

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:38.040
Haruka!

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:40.450
Don't, Yuu. You'll get pulled in
if you get too close!

00:22:40.850 --> 00:22:42.180
Yuu!

00:22:42.650 --> 00:22:43.820
Haruka!

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:49.150
Karasu!

00:22:50.740 --> 00:22:52.420
Haruka!

00:24:42.240 --> 00:24:44.270
I'm dreaming again.

00:24:45.240 --> 00:24:47.080
That summer day's dream.

00:24:47.950 --> 00:24:51.380
It's supposed to be
15 years into the future.

00:24:53.990 --> 00:24:56.350
But it's not necessary for me.

00:24:59.730 --> 00:25:02.090
Then come with me to Shangri-la!

00:25:04.300 --> 00:25:06.420
Next episode, Once More

00:25:07.530 --> 00:25:10.000
Will I see you again?
